{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488210-defense-and-armor-combined-for-antagonists-am-i-understanding-this-correctly","id":1488210,"title":"Defense and Armor Combined for Antagonists - Am I Understanding this correctly?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-27T14:33:16-07:00","id":1488210,"title":"Defense and Armor Combined for Antagonists - Am I Understanding this correctly?","content":"My first Aberrant game in the new system kicks off tomorrow, I am just going through the rules one more time and had a question. <br /> <br /> So by default, Soft Armor and Defense are combined into a single rating for Antagonists, correct? If so, does this mean:<ul><li>If I exceed an antagonist's Defense rating, the Inflict Damage stunt is free.</li> <li>If I have a Scale advantage over an Antagonist, allowing me to buy additional Inflict Damage stunts, are they also free? Or do I need to pay the full Defense rating in successes for each subsequent Inflict Damage stunt?</li> <li>When fighting novas, does this mean there is no distinction between a super-speed nova with five Defense from the Defense Mega-Edge, and a nova with five dots of Toughness? (Leave Scale aside for a second.) The first in theory has a high 'Defense' rating while the other has high 'Armor' in player terms, but these are all one stat for purpose of antagonists.</li> </ul>If I am reading this correctly, is the Inflict Damage stunt having a cost equal to armor effectively only something that comes into play when attacking a player character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T17:01:44-07:00","id":1488226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrApophenia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1488210-defense-and-armor-combined-for-antagonists-am-i-understanding-this-correctly#post1488210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If I exceed an antagonist's Defense rating, the Inflict Damage stunt is free.<br /> 2. If I have a Scale advantage over an Antagonist, allowing me to buy additional Inflict Damage stunts, are they also free? Or do I need to pay the full Defense rating in successes for each subsequent Inflict Damage stunt?<br /> 3. When fighting novas, does this mean there is no distinction between a super-speed nova with five Defense from the Defense Mega-Edge, and a nova with five dots of Toughness? (Leave Scale aside for a second.) The first in theory has a high 'Defense' rating while the other has high 'Armor' in player terms, but these are all one stat for purpose of antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Yes, you already payed for it.<br /> 2. Yes, all free.<br /> 3. Its up to you s SG. The point is, Antagonists are as complex or as simple as you want. If you are fighting a Nova, you probablu should pick the antagonist defense and split it into defense and armor. Storypath is meant to be simple to run, so if you dont want to ring this complexity to the fight you can avoid it, and for most fights you can (specially when the players are novas and the adversaries are not). But meaningful fights, when the characters may need to explore more than the damage side, or when the adversary should remainalive for long (or even scape at the end) you should bring armor, different stunts, enhancements for specific situations, things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 07-27-2022, 08:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}